+### 2026-09-29 (late) — PR #683 adjudicated, and the volatile root cause was not what either of us said
+
+Red-teamed the competing PR #683 (`582823799`, 53 files, +7885/−375, same base)
+by building both trees and running both PRs' gates against both binaries. Full
+write-up: [`engineering/PR683-ADJUDICATION.md`](../PR683-ADJUDICATION.md).
+
+**#683 beat this branch on the axis that matters.** Its
+`check_volatile_spin_loop.sh` pairs six volatile probes that must keep an access
+per iteration with three **non-volatile controls** that must be hoisted to zero,
+so a green run cannot mean "the compiler hoisted nothing at all". Mutation
+matrix, guard deleted from `hoist_loop_invariants` and both trees rebuilt:
+their `check_volatile_spin_loop.sh` and `check_volatile_licm.sh` exit 1 on both
+mutated builds; this branch's `check_volatile_pointer_subscript.sh` exits 1;
+**#683's** version of that same gate exits **0** — it counts memory operands
+function-wide, so a load hoisted out of the loop but still inside `spin`
+satisfies it. It is wired into CI as a safety net and does not catch the thing.
+They wrote the correct helper (`lib_loop_bounds.sh`) and used it in their two
+newer gates, but never retrofitted the inherited one. This also overturns my own
+earlier note that the audit's HIGH-1 was false: it was right about the gate it
+named, and my counter-evidence came from a gate #683 does not ship.
+
+**And the root cause was neither explanation.** The audit of #683 says rustc's
+`unused_variables` does not fire on refutable-pattern destructuring; I had
+written the same claim into this branch's docs. Both are wrong — measured with a
+two-variant enum and the lint forced on, rustc names the binding and suggests
+`volatile: _`. The real cause is the crate-wide `#![allow(unused_variables, …)]`
+in `src/lib.rs`, which also explains why `-D warnings` changed nothing and why
+`cargo fix` offers "89 suggestions" while applying none. **The allow is now
+removed**, all 99 resulting warnings across 49 files are resolved, and with the
+guard deleted `./scripts/build_lccc_fast.sh` fails with
+`error: unused variable: 'volatile' --> src/passes/licm.rs:1256:30`. The
+miscompile can no longer ship, for every destructured safety flag in the crate
+rather than just `volatile`. Its blind spot is recorded: `if false && *volatile`
